# NEON HARBOR — Open-World Crime Game

[![make.fun bounty](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![rank](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/roymaster46/neon-harbor/rank.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)
[![reward](https://make.fun/badge/gta6-01/roymaster46/neon-harbor/reward.svg)](https://make.fun/bounty/gta6-01?utm_source=github&utm_medium=readme&utm_campaign=gta6-01)

**Neon Harbor** is an original 3D open-world crime game set in a rain-soaked
neon port city that never sleeps. You are **Rook**, getaway driver for the
harbor crew. One night, ten jobs, one last ferry — and a 5-star police force
with helicopters, roadblocks and spike strips trying to end the run before
dawn. The game boots straight into the middle of the chase: Mission 6,
stage 3 of 4, four stars up, a police helicopter overhead and a roadblock
on Harbor Bridge.

Everything is original: the city, characters, vehicles, story and sounds.
No Rockstar / GTA names, characters, map, art or music are used. All art is
procedural Three.js geometry with canvas-generated textures, all sound is
synthesized with WebAudio, and the game ships as plain static files and makes
**zero network requests** at runtime (Three.js r160 is vendored under
`game/vendor/`).

## The city

A 960×960 m open world on a street grid: ten districts — Pier 9, Harbor
Bridge, Neon Row, Downtown, Old Port, Marina, Warehouse Row, Uptown, Canal
Side and Northgate — each with its own neon colour on the HUD and minimap.
A black harbor with container cranes, a six-lane bridge with pink and cyan
edge neon, wet streets that mirror the signs, rain that never stops, and
lightning over the bay. Landmarks you will learn by heart: Club Mirage,
Vex Garage, Harbor Arms, The Pearl Casino, the Pier 9 cranes and the Ferry
Terminal.

## The hook: one night, ten jobs

Every mission is a set piece in the rain: a cab fare that turns into a
recruitment, a casino garage heist, a canal smuggling run, a dockside deal
that goes south, a midnight street race, the Harbor Bridge chase, the Pearl
Casino vault, a convoy ambush on the Northgate highway, a storm-surge
escape, and the last boat out. Each mission pays cash and respect.

## Systems

- **On foot** — WASD to move, Shift to sprint. Camera follows behind you.
  Press E near a parked car to steal it (that is a crime — the NHPD notices).
- **Cars** — 7 cars, from the Harbor Cab to the Harbor One hypercar, plus
  live traffic on the road grid. Drive with WASD/arrows, Shift for
  handbrake, N for nitro (top speed ×1.65, ×1.85 with the Nitro Kit).
  Cars take damage, dent, and can be wrecked.
- **Police, 5 stars** — wanted level rises with every crime and decays when
  you stay hidden. 1–2 stars: patrol cars chase and ram you. 3+: a police
  helicopter joins with a searchlight. 4+: roadblocks. 5 stars: spike
  strips, the helicopter and roadblocks together. Bribe them at any time
  (button in the HUD) — the price scales with your stars.
- **Combat** — 4 weapons (Fists, .38 Harbor, HK-9 SMG, 12G Breacher) with a
  weapon wheel (Q) and slots (1–4), ammo, falloff damage, and police cars
  that take damage, smoke, and can be disabled. Kevlar vests absorb 70% of
  damage before health.
- **Story missions** — 10 staged missions (M to open the list), each with
  stages, a live beacon, a crew dialog line with a portrait, and a payout.
- **Crew** — recruit Mira (driver, nitro lasts 50% longer), Vex (mechanic,
  half-price repairs) and Kiki (lookout, wanted decays twice as fast).
  Each has a real gameplay perk and a key (Z / X / C).
- **Garage & shop** — Vex Garage (G) sells cars and upgrades: tuned
  engines, nitro kits, plated bodies, grip tires, repairs, plus the
  safehouse heal. Harbor Arms (B) sells weapons, ammo, armor — and recruits
  crew.
- **Respect & rank** — earn respect from missions and jobs to climb from
  Nobody to Runner, Wheelman, Fixer, Hustler, Harbor Legend and King of the
  Harbor.
- **Side jobs** — taxi fares (T), courier runs (C) and vigilante hits (V),
  all paying cash and respect.
- **A living harbor** — 12 traffic cars cruising the grid, 22 pedestrians
  who panic and flee when the heat rises, a storm that deepens through the
  night, falling rain, lightning, and a police dispatch panel that names
  every unit, its tactic and its live distance from you.
- **Radio** — 4 synthesized stations (R to cycle): NEON 101 synthwave,
  STORM FM night drive, HARBOR TALK evacuation watch, WAVE 90.4 island pop.
  All music is generated live by WebAudio — no audio files — plus a
  synthesized engine hum that follows your speed and a two-tone siren when
  the helicopter is up.
- **Save** — autosaves every 20 seconds and on demand (Save button) to
  localStorage; progress, money, weapons, cars, crew and missions persist.

## Controls

| Key | Action |
| --- | ------ |
| WASD / arrows | Move / drive |
| Shift | Sprint / handbrake |
| Mouse click | Shoot |
| E | Interact / steal car / exit car |
| Q / 1–4 | Weapon wheel / weapon slots |
| N | Nitro |
| B | Gun shop |
| G | Safehouse / garage |
| M | Mission list |
| R | Cycle radio |
| V | Vigilante job |
| T | Taxi job |
| C | Courier job |
| P / Esc | Pause |

## Play it

```sh
node serve.ts
# open http://localhost:8080
```

## Tests

```sh
node --test tests/logic.test.mjs
```

